window.docContents[220].resolve({"/Type-systems/#Core-C______--Type-systems":{"contents":"Overloading of functions and methods by the type of the arguments, operator members, class templates instantiated by substitution, subtyping and type inference.\n\nA name denotes an overload set, and a call selects one candidate. An infix operator on an object, and the indexing of an object, are the calls of the members operator⊕ and operator[]. A member may return , so v[i] = x assigns to the location operator[] returns.\n\nA template is expanded before the program is checked, so instantiation costs nothing at run time. Only the instantiations are checked.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Core C++","header":"7. Type systems","id":"/Type-systems/#Core-C______--Type-systems"}});